  "text": "Veterinary Oncology Luton | Davies Vet Specialists\nPet Owners\n>\nMeet Our Team\nBeing referred to Davies\nFacilities\nThe Referral Process\nFact Sheets\nFAQ\nClient Care\nFinance and Insurance\nSustainability\nVet Professionals\n>\nAppointment Request Form\nEmergency Referrals\nRadiology Request Form\nTPLO Post Op Form\nBook CPD\nCPD Webinar Library\nPopular Downloads\nServices\n>\nAnaesthesia\nCardiology\nDentistry & Maxillofacial Surgery\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency and Critical Care\nHearing Assessment Clinic\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nNursing\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTherapy Services\nClient Care\nOur Team\n>\nAnaesthesia Team\nCardiology Team\nClient Care Team\nDentistry & Maxillofacial Surgery Team\nDermatology Team\nEmergency & Critical Care Team\nDiagnostic Imaging Team\nGreen Group\nHearing Clinic Team\nFinance Team\nInternal Medicine Team\nInterns\nLeadership Team\nNeurology Team\nNursing Team\nOncology Team\nOphthalmology Team\nOrthopaedics Team\nPain Management Team\nPatient Care Assistants and Technicians\nTherapy Services Team\nSoft Tissue Surgery Team\nSupport Team\nJoin Our Team\nContact Us\nInsights\n>\nBlogs\nNews\nFact Sheets\nCase Studies\nNewsletters\nCPD\nEmergencies\n01582 883950\nRefer Here\nLog In / Register\nUPDATE: Please be aware that our opening hours have changed on Monday 19th September. Please contact us for any emergency care.\nVeterinary Oncology Luton\nWhat is\nVeterinary Oncology Luton\n?\nVeterinary oncology\nis the care of pets with cancer. Our specialist team of oncologists support pets and their owners in this distressing time with treatment plans and professional advice following a diagnosis of cancer. At Davies Veterinary Specialists, we have an entire team that takes care of patients with cancer, and our facilities house our specialist equipment that identifies the cancer as well as treats it.\nAt Davies Veterinary Specialists, our oncology team is here to provide compassionate support every step of the way. We focus on preserving your pet’s quality of life, offering comprehensive care from diagnosis and treatment to palliative support, allowing them to enjoy as much of a normal life as possible.\nPrioritising Life with\nVeterinary Oncology Luton\nThe philosophy of our\npet oncology service\nis to ensure every pet we see maintains the best quality of life during treatment. In many cases, combinations of medical and surgical treatment can have very positive outcomes on quality of life. We are also able to treat cancer through various means, including drugs (\nchemotherapy\nand tyrosine kinase inhibitors), the melanoma vaccine (Oncept) therapy and surgery. The diagnosis and treatment of cancer requires input from other disciplines within the hospital, so our oncologists work very closely with soft tissue surgeons and other clinical services teams.\nDiagnosing Cancer in Pets:\nVeterinary Oncology Luton\nDavies Veterinary Specialists in Luton utilise advanced methods in our oncology services to ensure accurate diagnosis and effective treatment of cancer in pets.\nWe firstly offer thorough clinical examinations, followed by state-of-the-art diagnostic techniques such as digital imaging (X-rays, CT scans, and ultrasound), fine-needle aspirates, and biopsies to confirm cancer type and stage.\nMolecular diagnostics and cytology are also employed for precise analysis. Once diagnosed, the team develops personalised treatment plans which may include chemotherapy, surgery, immunotherapy, or palliative care, depending on the pet’s condition and needs.\nMake a Referral Today\nTreatment Services with\nVeterinary Oncology Luton\nOur oncology service benefits from the expertise of European Veterinary Specialists in\nanaesthesia,\nneurology\n,\northopaedics\n,\nand\nsoft tissue surgery\n, enabling us to perform complex cancer surgeries, from thoracic and abdominal procedures to specialised oral and spinal surgeries. Our long-standing\nchemotherapy\nclinic, led by skilled nurses and oncologists, provides personalised and compassionate care. We treat a wide range of cancers, offering chemotherapy\nas a standalone treatment or in combination with surgery and radiotherapy.\nWhy Choose Davies for Your\nVeterinary Oncology Luton\nReferrals?\nPartnering with a team of leading experts –\nNot only are we specialists, but our facilities are exceptional for diagnosing and caring for your pets.\nExtensive experience in diagnosing and treating –\nOur team diagnoses and treats a wide range of cancer types.\nComprehensive\nrange of therapies\n–\nsuch as chemotherapy, surgery, and palliative care, all delivered with compassion and a focus on quality of life.\nClear communication, collaborative case management, and access to cutting-edge treatments\n– we work well alongside primary practices and support pet owners when needed. We deliver timely results and foster a safe environment.\nGet Referrals for a Veterinary Oncologist Luton\nRegular veterinary check-ups are essential for the early detection and management of cancers. If you notice any of the signs in your pet, it’s important to consult with your veterinarian as soon as possible. We receive vet referrals for\nveterinary oncology Luton\nand referrals from pet owners, but consulting your usual vet for the symptoms your pet is showing is important to find the right solution or area of concern.\nSee our page here for Veterinary Cardiologist Luton\nMake a Referral Today\nMake a Referral Today\nOur Facilities\nOur small animal referral hospital is designed to ensure that the very best veterinary care can be provided 24 hours a day.\nRead More\nAbout Us\nAt Davies Veterinary Specialists we've been delivering outstanding care to small animals for over 20 years.\nRead More\nCase Studies\nChallenging cases, innovative treatments or just a great outcome for all. Read some of our patients' stories in our case studies.\nRead More\nDavies Veterinary Specialists FAQs\nAll your questions about Davies Veterinary Specialists - answered.\nRead More\nBlogs\nRead the latest blogs from the team at Davies Veterinary Specialists.\nRead More\nContact Us\nMap, Sat Nav, Opening Times and all our contact details.\nRead More\nNeed to make a referral?\nGet in touch with us using the form below.\nRefer Now\nAnaesthesia\nCardiology\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nPet Hearing Assessment Clinic\nInternal Medicine\nVeterinary Neurology and Neurosurgery\nVeterinary Nursing\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTherapy and Fitness Services\nVeterinary Client Care\nAbout Us\nDavies Veterinary Specialists FAQs\nJoin Our Team\nSustainability\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited trading as Davies Veterinary Specialists\nManor Farm Business Park\n|\nHigham Gobion\n|\nHertfordshire\n|\nSG5 3HR\n|\nTel 01582 883950\nRegistered address: Friars Gate 1011 Stratford Road Solihull B90 4BN\n|\nRegistered in England & Wales 10790375\n|\nVAT Reg 195 092 877\nCookie Settings\n© 2026 Davies Veterinary Specialists,\nPart of Linnaeus, an Affiliate of Mars, Incorporated\nHosting and Maintenance by Clickingmad\nTerms of Service (New)\nTerms of Service (Old)\nLegal Notice\nPrivacy Statement\nCookies Policy\nModern Slavery Act\nCustomer Charter\nComplaints\nGender Pay Gap Report\nAccessibility\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited trading as Davies Veterinary Specialists\n01582 883950\n©2026 Davies Veterinary Specialists",
